      <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Quantitative results (Baseline and Ablation) on ActCutBench / ActCutBench-Lite. <strong class="text-white/80">NC</strong> Narrative Consistency for Global Text-Visual Alignment (<em>Env</em>: Environment, <em>Sce</em>: Scene, <em>Sty</em>: Style, <em>CS</em>: Character Setting, <em>CA/OM</em>: Character Action / Object Motion). <strong class="text-white/80">VC</strong> Visual Coherence for Inter-shots Static Visual Similarity (<em>Env</em>, <em>Sce</em>, <em>Sty</em>, <em>CS</em>). <strong class="text-white/80">AC</strong> Action Continuity for Adjacent-shots Dynamic Visual Continuity (<em>CA/OM</em>). <strong class="text-white/80">SC</strong> Subject Correctness for Single-shot Local Text-Visual Alignment (<em>CC</em>: Character Count, <em>CID</em>: Character Identity, both derived from FoA: Focus-of-Attention). <strong class="text-white/80">SA</strong> Shot Alignment for Multi-shot Structural Integrity (<em>SCC</em>: Shot Count Correctness, <em>SCA</em>: Shot Cutting Accuracy). <strong class="text-white/80">Aes</strong> Aesthetics Score for Visual Quality. All metrics ↑ higher is better.
      </p>
    </div>
